-- title:
--   Transfer from a finite-index normal subgroup of a free group
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a group which is free (as a `IsFreeGroup` structure), let $R \le F$ be a normal subgroup of finite index, and assume that every commutator $xyx^{-1}y^{-1}$ of elements of $F$ lies in $R$, so that $F/R$ is abelian. Let $A$ be an abelian group, and give the set $R \to^* A$ of group homomorphisms from $R$ to $A$ its pointwise abelian group structure. The assertion has two parts. First, the transfer map $\chi \mapsto \mathrm{transfer}\,\chi$, sending a homomorphism $\chi : R \to A$ to the corresponding homomorphism $F \to A$, is surjective: every homomorphism $F \to A$ is the transfer of some homomorphism $R \to A$. Second, for $\chi : R \to A$ the transfer of $\chi$ is trivial if and only if $\chi$ lies in the subgroup of $R \to^* A$ generated by the set of all homomorphisms of the form $r \mapsto \chi'(grg^{-1})\,\chi'(r)^{-1}$, where $g$ ranges over $F$ (acting on $R$ through the conjugation automorphism `MulAut.conjNormal g` of the normal subgroup $R$) and $\chi'$ ranges over $R \to^* A$.
--
--   This is the statement that, for a free group $F$ and a finite-index normal subgroup $R$ with abelian quotient, corestriction $H^1(R,A) \to H^1(F,A)$ is surjective with kernel the augmentation subgroup, i.e. that it identifies the $F/R$-coinvariants of $\mathrm{Hom}(R,A)$ with $\mathrm{Hom}(F,A)$. It is used in the study of the degree homomorphism on the cohomological carrier, in [`CohCarrier.surjective_jDeg_one_and_jDeg_eq_zero_iff_of_four_le`](thm.html#CohCarrier.surjective_jDeg_one_and_jDeg_eq_zero_iff_of_four_le).
